For the first time, the decay $\Xi_{cc}^{++} \rightarrow \Xi_{c}^{+} \pi^{+}$ has been observed with a statistical significance of $5.9\sigma$, validating a recent detection of this baryon in the $\Lambda_c^{+} K^{-} \pi^{+} \pi^{+}$ channel. This result is based on a dataset with an integrated luminosity of $1.7\,\mathrm{fb}^{-1}$ gathered by the LHCb experiment from proton-proton collisions at a center-of-mass energy of $13\,\mathrm{TeV}$. The mass of the $\Xi_{cc}^{++}$ is determined to be
\begin{equation}\nonumber
3620.6\pm 1.5~(\text{stat})\pm 0.4~(\text{syst}) \pm
0.3~(\Xi_{c}^{+})~\text{MeV}/\it{c}^{2},
\end{equation}
which aligns with earlier findings. Additionally, the ratio of branching fractions for the decay modes is measured as
\begin{equation}\nonumber
\frac{\mathcal{B} (\Xi_{cc}^{++} \rightarrow \Xi_{c}^{+} \pi^{+}) \times
\mathcal{B}(\Xi_{c}^{+} \rightarrow pK^{-}\pi^{+})}
  {\mathcal{B} (\Xi_{cc}^{++} \rightarrow \Lambda_c^{+} K^{-} \pi^{+} \pi^{+})
\times \mathcal{B}(\Lambda_c^{+} \rightarrow pK^{-}\pi^{+})}
  = 0.035\pm 0.009~(\text{stat}) \pm 0.003~(\text{syst}).
\end{equation}

